      "role": "user",
      "content": "got it. so the civil liberties stuff is mostly about autonomy and legal precedent. but when it comes to the actual science, though... it feels like the scientific side's arguments are way more concrete and backed by data, whereas the skepticism side seems a bit more like they're just picking at holes in the consensus. do you think there's actually any scientific merit to the claims that mandates are counterproductive for public health, or is that mostly just a political argument?",
